> How do I make a line in R's plot_ly that I've added with add_lines dashed and with a given color?
**assistant**:
> To make a line dashed and set its color in R's `plot_ly`, you can use the `add_lines` function and specify the `line` argument with appropriate properties. Here's an example:
> 
> ```r
> library(plotly)
> 
> # Sample data
> x <- c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)
> y <- c(2, 3, 5, 4, 6)
> 
> # Create a plot with dashed line and specified color
> plot <- plot_ly(x = ~x, y = ~y) %>%
>   add_lines(line = list(dash = 'dash', color = 'red')) # Set line properties
> 
> plot
> ```
> 
> In this example:
> - `dash = 'dash'` specifies the line style as dashed.
> - `color = 'red'` sets the line color. You can replace `'red'` with any valid color name or color code you prefer.
> 
> You can also explore other line properties like width by adjusting the `line` list as needed.
