> I can use marker= even if I added the bar with add_bars?
**assistant**:
> Yes, you can use the `marker` argument with `add_bars`. The `marker` argument allows you to customize the appearance of the bars, including their color. Here’s how you can do it:
> 
> ```r
> library(plotly)
> 
> # Sample data
> categories <- c("A", "B", "C", "D")
> values <- c(10, 15, 7, 12)
> 
> # Create a bar plot using add_bars with the same color for all bars
> plot <- plot_ly() %>%
>   add_bars(x = ~categories, y = ~values, 
>            marker = list(color = 'green')) # Set bar color
> 
> plot
> ```
> 
> In this example, by using `marker = list(color = 'green')`, all the bars will appear in green, regardless of how they are added (using `add_bars`). You can customize the color to fit your design or presentation needs!
